window.docContents[9].resolve({"/rules/RG1003/#RG1003-fix":{"contents":"1. Inspect the declaration's axiom list in the diagnostic or with #print axioms, and follow it to the declaration that introduces the axiom.2. Replace the axiom in the dependency with a proof, or make it a hypothesis of the results that need it.3. If the dependency cannot change, do not claim the affected declarations on a conforming surface.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG1003: Unknown transitive axioms are forbidden","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/RG1003/#RG1003-fix"},"/rules/RG2002/#RG2002-fix":{"contents":"1. Remove or correct unknown keys and invalid values; the diagnostic names them.2. Add each root library and executable to surfaces or to the matching exclusion array, with a rationale.3. A claimed executable must be a standalone root such as Main; its root module cannot belong to a manifested library.4. Run lake lint -- --explain-config to see the manifest, scope, profiles and stages the driver would use, without auditing.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG2002: Configuration must classify the complete Lake surface","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/RG2002/#RG2002-fix"},"/rules/RG3001/#RG3001-fix":{"contents":"1. Remove metaprogramming commands from modules whose implemented_by history must be authenticated, or move them elsewhere.2. Ensure every dependency's compiled code is available in the build.3. Break cycles consisting only of replacement edges.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG3001: Execution closure must have no unresolved paths","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/RG3001/#RG3001-fix"}});